      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we can use the tangent addition formula. The tangent addition formula states:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\n\nWe can use the fact that \\(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ = 45^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we can write:\n\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\). Expanding this expression, we have:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFrom the previous equation, we know that \\(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + 1 = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
