      "text": "To solve the expression \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we can use trigonometric identities. Specifically, we will use the tangent addition formula and some properties of angles.\n\nFirst, recall the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\n\nLet \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\). Then:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ\n\\]\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nThis gives us the equation:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by \\(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nSimplifying, we have:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ (1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ (1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 - \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nFrom this, we can see that:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ (1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)}\n\\]\nNow, we need to find the value of \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\). Let:\n\\[\nx = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = 1 + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThen:\n\\[\nx y = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nFrom our earlier result, we know:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting this into the equation for \\(xy\\), we get:\n\\[\nx y = 1 + 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 2 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 2\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
